# Golden case set for the Disputes and Chargebacks Manager (F2). Obviously fictional data only.
#
# Each line is ONE labelled scenario keyed by `kind`. The `expected_*` field on every line is the
# INDEPENDENT ORACLE: it is hand-declared from the client policy (filing windows, abuse bands,
# intended lifecycle), NOT read back from the pipeline. A metric scores the engine's answer
# AGAINST that label, so a wrong engine turns the metric red. The metrics and their homes:
#
#   kind=eligibility -> eligibility_accuracy : engine verdict vs expected_eligible
#   kind=abuse       -> abuse_accuracy       : engine outcome vs expected_outcome
#   kind=intake      -> intake_accuracy      : model classification vs expected_category
#   kind=lifecycle   -> lifecycle_trace      : state-machine replay vs expected_states
#   kind=grounded    -> groundedness         : every figure in the drafted pack is engine-sourced
#   kind=pii         -> pii_safety           : no raw identifier survives redact-before-audit
#
# `run_eval.py` also proves every one of these metrics can go RED (agent_eval_kit) before scoring.
#
# --- eligibility: card-scheme window 120d (10.4/13.1/13.3); retail 30d (R-REFUND) / 45d (R-INR);
#     an unknown reason code and a negative filing age both fail closed (ineligible). ---
